        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "chk_doc_9388_1",
        "documentId": "doc_93885f20c9aff7b3",
        "chunkIndex": 1,
        "text": "Module III: Solution of Algebraic and Transcendental Equations\n20 Introduction, Bisection Method, Regula Falsi Method, Secant Method, Iteration Method, Newton Raphson\nMethod, Rate of Convergence\nModule IV: Interpolation and Curve Fitting\n20 Types of Operators, Basic Definition, Forward Differences, Backward Differences, Central Differences,\nNewton Forward/Backward/Central Differences Formula, Newton’s Divided Difference Formula, Lagrange’s\nMethod. Module V: Numerical Differentiation & Integration\n15\nNumerical Differentiation based on Interpolation Formula, Numerical Integration, Trapezoidal Rule,\nSimpson’s 1/3 rule, Simpson’s 3/8 Rule, Weddle’s Rule. Module VI: Numerical Solution to ODE\n15 Basic Definition, Euler’s Method, Modified Euler’s Method, Runga Kutta Method (2nd and 4th Order)\nStudent Learning Outcomes:\nAfter completion of the course,the student will be able to:\nExplain concept of various numerical methods, in particular, with reference to numerical solution of non linear equations and system\nof linear equations, interpolation, numerical differentiation and integration and numerical solution of ordinary differential equations. Apply important theorems. Use different formulae for various numerical methods to be covered with an aim of understand the fundamentals, concepts and\npractical use of these methods in the field of computer sciences and applications.",
