        "id": "msg_af47671c64c9",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "**LibrAI Technical Reference & Architecture Manual**\n\n**Overview and Core Architecture**\n\nLibrAI is a high-performance AI Document Assistant designed for digital libraries, assessment tools, and enterprise document intelligence. Its decoupled layered architecture consists of:\n\n1. Ingestion Pipeline: High-speed PDF/TXT parsing with UTF-8 normalization and page offset indexing.\n2. Semantic Chunking: Sentence-boundary packaging with an 800-token target size and a 120-token sliding overlap window.\n3. Hybrid Retrieval: Combining BM25 keyword matching with dense vector similarity and Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF).\n4. Redis Caching & Rate Limiting: Utilizing sliding-window rate limiters, multi-turn conversation session stores with configurable TTL, and normalized query response caching.\n\n**Retrieval Strategies and Context Management**\n\nTo prevent context overflow and model hallucination:\n\n* Only top-k highest scoring passages (default: 4 chunks) are passed to the LLM system prompt.\n* Conversation history is trimmed dynamically to maintain strict adherence to model context limits (max 1,200 history tokens).\n* The prompt enforces strict negative grounding: if a user's question cannot be completely answered by the context, the model explicitly refuses to speculate.\n\n**Evidence Mode & Grounding Verification**\n\nLibrAI's unique \"Evidence Mode\" feature provides:\n\n* Exact character excerpt extraction and chunk citations.\n* Automated confidence score calculated from BM25 and semantic similarity weights.\n* Grounding status classification: 'supported' (confidence >= 0.45), 'insufficient' (low confidence or missing evidence), or 'unsupported' (irrelevant query).\n\n**Performance Benchmarks and Scalability**\n\nUnder typical production loads:\n\n* Cache hits return in under 15ms with the header \"cached: true\".\n* Chunking processes 100 pages of text in under 450ms.\n* Hybrid BM25 lookup evaluates across 10,000 chunks in sub-8ms latency.\n* Supported file types include PDF, TXT, and Markdown files up to 10MB in size.",
