        "content": "**Course Overview**\n\nThe document appears to be a course syllabus for a Computer Oriented Numerical Analysis course, denoted as DSC307, at the undergraduate level.\n\n**Course Objectives**\n\nThe course aims to cover the theory and application of numerical approximation techniques, including numerical error, root-finding, interpolation, and polynomial approximation.\n\n**Course Structure**\n\nThe course is divided into six modules:\n\n1. Introduction to Numerical Analysis\n2. Solution of Linear Algebraic Equations\n3. Numerical Differentiation and Integration\n4. Numerical Solution of Ordinary Differential Equations\n5. Interpolation and Curve Fitting\n6. Applications of Numerical Methods\n\n**Assessment Scheme**\n\nThe course assessment is divided into two parts:\n\n1. Theory and Examination (75%)\n2. Lab/Practical/Studio Assessment (25%)\n\n**Textbooks and References**\n\nThe recommended textbooks for the course are:\n\n1. Mollah S. A., Numerical Analysis and Computational Procedures\n2. Sastry S. S., Introductory Methods of Numerical Analysis\n3. Jain M. K., Iyengar S. R. K., Jain R. K., Numerical Methods: For Scientific and Engineering Computation\n\n**Additional Resources**\n\nThe course also includes references to other textbooks and authors, including Rajaraman V, Krishnamurthy, E.V., Sen, S.K, and Stoer, Bullrich.",
